   This grant does not by itself permit you to USE the Licensed Work, or any
   derivative of it, to compute a result. Use is governed by sections 2 and 3.

2. Academic Use Grant

   You may use the Licensed Work free of charge for Educational Purposes and
   for Academic Research.

   2.1 "Educational Purposes" means teaching, coursework, classroom
       demonstration, and self-study, by students and by educators at an
       Educational Institution, or by an individual learning the subject.

   2.2 "Academic Research" means research carried out at an Educational
       Institution by its students, faculty or research staff, where the
       results may be published openly.

       Academic Research includes publishing those results — in a paper,
       preprint, thesis, dissertation, poster or talk — subject to the
       acknowledgement in section 2.5.

   2.3 "Educational Institution" means a university, college, school, or
       other institution whose primary purpose is education and which grants
       academic degrees or recognised qualifications, including a research
       institute or laboratory operated by and forming part of such an
       institution.

       It does not mean a company, a government or national research
       institute that is not part of an Educational Institution, a hospital
       or clinical body operating commercially, or a non-profit whose primary
       purpose is not education. Those are not excluded from using the
       Licensed Work — see section 3, and please ask; Licensor is willing to
       grant them terms.

   2.4 The Academic Use Grant does NOT cover:

       (a) research carried out for, or funded by, a commercial sponsor where
           the sponsor receives results that are confidential, or exclusive
           rights in them. Openly published research remains covered even if
           it was grant-funded;
       (b) consultancy, contract testing, or any service provided to a third
           party for a fee;
       (c) use by a spin-out, start-up or other commercial entity, whatever
           its relationship to the institution;
       (d) any use in the design, certification, operation or assessment of a
           real product, plant, building or system, whoever performs it.

   2.5 If you publish results obtained with the Licensed Work, acknowledge it.
       A citation of this form is sufficient:

           meteor-cfd, 주식회사 메테오시뮬레이션 (Meteo Simulation Co., Ltd.),
           https://github.com/using76/meteor-cfd

       This is a condition of the grant in section 2, not a request.

3. Licensed Use

   Any use of the Licensed Work outside section 2 requires a separate
   commercial licence from Licensor. This includes, without limitation:

     * research and development inside a company, at any scale;
     * research at a government or national research institute that is not
       part of an Educational Institution;
     * evaluation for procurement;
     * consultancy, contract research, and testing services;
     * any production, operational or commercial use.

   Commercial licences are available. Please write to simul@msimul.com with a
   description of the intended use, and Licensor will respond with terms.

   If you are unsure which side of section 2 your use falls on — a national
   laboratory, a hospital research group, a non-profit, a university spin-out,
   a sponsored project — write and ask. Licensor would rather answer the
   question than have you guess, and grants no-cost or reduced-cost licences
   where the use is not commercial in substance.

4. Redistribution

